# Architecture: Custom Store Pattern

## Context

This app uses a minimal custom state store (`app/src/store.ts`) with a
dispatch/subscribe engine. State flows unidirectionally:
action creators → `store.dispatch(action)` → reducer → new state → listeners.

This is NOT Redux, Zustand, MobX, Jotai, or any third-party state library.
Do not "modernize" it by introducing one.

## Rule

- ALL state changes MUST go through `store.dispatch(action)`.
- NEVER mutate `state` directly — the reducer returns a new object/array.
- New actions: first add a variant to the `Action` union in `app/src/types.ts`,
  then handle it in `app/src/reducer.ts`, then add an action creator in
  `app/src/actions.ts`.
- UI/components read state via selectors (`app/src/selectors.ts`), never by
  reaching into `state.tasks` or `state.filter` directly.
- DO NOT import or install Redux, Zustand, MobX, Jotai, or any external state
  management library.
- DO NOT add middleware, thunks, sagas, or async dispatch wrappers to the store.

## How to verify

1. `grep -r "state\." app/src/ --include="*.ts" | grep -v "state\." | grep "="` — no direct mutations outside the reducer.
2. `grep -rE "redux|zustand|mobx|jotai|recoil" app/` — should find zero matches.
3. Every new action type appears in `types.ts` Action union AND has a case in `reducer.ts`.
4. `grep -r "store.dispatch" app/src/` confirms dispatch is the only write path.
